WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.932
Step five checks the scope
against the fictional

2
00:00:02.932 --> 00:00:05.462
tenant and builds the
plan, sending nothing.

3
00:00:05.462 --> 00:00:10.583
The tenant check finds no findings and
two information items: Legacy Reports

4
00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:15.063
and Build Pipeline are eligible but
not Tier 1, so they're not in scope.

5
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:20.849
The plan has three creates, one no change,
one update and one not in repository.

6
00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:22.950
The named location is an update.

7
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.825
Ring 1's location policy
already exists and matches.

8
00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:30.200
Ring 1's risk policy and
both of Ring 2's are new.

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.767
And a policy someone made in the portal is

10
00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.788
reported as not in the
repository, and left alone.

11
00:00:35.788 --> 00:00:40.075
The dry run writes its four requests
to a file and sends none of them.

12
00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:42.140
You'd rerun with apply to send them.
